# 0008. Slash commands and @mentions

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-24

The console should feel like Claude Code: type to chat, `/` for commands, `@` to address.
This ADR fixes the command set and input grammar for v1.

## Technical details
- Input grammar: a line starting with `/` is a command; otherwise a message. Leading
  `@<id>` tokens set recipients (`@codex`, `@claude @llama`, `@all`); none means the
  default model. `\/` escapes a literal slash.
- Completion: `/` and `@` open a popup filtered as you type (commands; enabled model ids).
- Commands are a static table (`name, args, help, handler`), so `/help` is generated.

| Group | Command | Does |
|---|---|---|
| Session | `/help` | list commands |
| | `/clear` | start a new thread |
| | `/resume` | pick a past thread |
| | `/fork` | branch the current thread here |
| | `/exit` | quit (also `Ctrl-D` on empty input) |
| Info | `/usage [today\|thread\|all]` | tokens and cost per model, from the log |
| | `/context [id]` | what each participant has seen and how full its window is |
| | `/status` | each participant: up, unavailable (why), CLI version |
| Models | `/models` | list: id, kind, role, enabled |
| | `/model add` | guided form, writes `models.toml` and keychain |
| | `/model enable <id>` / `/model disable <id>` | see [0006](0006-model-registry-config.adr) |
| | `/model use <id>` | set default recipient |
| | `/model test <id>` | one-token ping, shows latency or the error |
| Talk | `/talk on\|off` | global switch for model-to-model talk |
| | `/talk allow <a>-><b>` / `/talk deny <a>-><b>` | edit the matrix |
| | `/talk show` | print the matrix |
| | `/budget <tokens>` / `/turns <n>` | per-message limits ([0007](0007-model-to-model-communication.adr)) |
| Context | `/compact [id]` | summarize history for a chat-only model to fit its window |
| | `/handoff <id>` | send a summary of the thread to `<id>` and make it default |

- Keys: `Enter` send, `Shift-Enter` newline, `Esc` cancel running replies, `Ctrl-C`
  twice quits, `Tab` cycles panes, `PgUp/PgDn` scroll, `Enter` on a handoff expands it.
- `/context` for CLI agents shows what roundtable sent and the usage they reported; it
  cannot show what the agent kept after its own compaction, and says so.
- Commands that change config write it at once and log a `status` event.

- Release order:
  - v1: `/help` `/clear` `/resume` `/exit`, `/models` `/model enable|disable|use|test`,
    `/usage` `/status` `/context`;
  - with `ask` ([0007](0007-model-to-model-communication.adr)): the whole Talk group,
    `/talk off` included;
  - later: `/model add` (guided setup; until then, edit `models.toml`), `/compact`,
    `/handoff`, `/fork` (see [0003](0003-sqlite-event-log.adr)).

Consequences: a familiar surface, discoverable through `/help` and completion. Cost: a
large surface overall, delivered in the order above.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: tui-textarea, ratatui popup widgets
- Alternatives: a separate command mode (vim-style `:`): less familiar to Claude Code users; flags at launch only: no live control
